senses
  entry
    definition "fail to keep or to maintain; cease to have, either physically or in an abstract sense"
    examples ("She lost her purse when she left it unattended on her seat")
    id oewn-02292634-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "fail to win"
    examples ("We lost the battle but we won the war")
    id oewn-01102003-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "suffer the loss of a person through death or removal"
    examples ("She lost her husband in the war" "The couple that wanted to adopt the child lost her when the biological parents claimed her")
    id oewn-01799093-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "miss from one's possessions; lose sight of"
    examples ("I've lost my glasses again!")
    id oewn-02292463-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "allow to go out of sight or mind"
    examples ("The detective lost the man he was shadowing after he had to stop at a red light" "lose the crowds by climbing a mountain" "the lost tribe")
    id oewn-02201537-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "fail to make money in a business; make a loss or fail to profit"
    examples ("I lost thousands of dollars on that bad investment!" "The company turned a loss after the first year")
    id oewn-02293733-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose "turn a loss")
  entry
    definition "fail to get or obtain"
    examples ("I lost the opportunity to spend a year abroad")
    id oewn-02293000-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "fail to perceive or to catch with the senses or the mind"
    examples ("I missed that remark" "She missed his point" "We lost part of what he said")
    id oewn-02132318-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (miss lose)
  entry
    definition "withdraw, as from reality"
    examples ("he lost himself in his music")
    id oewn-00497220-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "be set at a disadvantage"
    examples ("This author really suffers in translation" "The painting loses something in this light")
    id oewn-00205234-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (suffer lose)
